// @emit-error emitProgram: parameter `T[]` still names an unsubstituted type parameter — a lambda declared inside a generic body keeps the enclosing `T`, so its signature is interned at the unsubstituted type; give the lambda a concrete parameter type or take the value from the enclosing scope
// GRADUATED from `silent-class-inventory` D426 — a lambda declared INSIDE a generic body,
// whose own parameter annotation still names the enclosing `T`.
//
// THE SIGNATURE IS WRONG, NOT THE REFUSAL. `monoCloneBody` rebuilds an instance's statement
// spine and leaves a nested lambda's annotation alone — its header says so in as many words
// — and `collectFns` has already lifted that lambda, so ONE lifted function serves every
// instance and its `$fnsig` is interned at the unsubstituted type. Disassembled, master's
// module calls `call_indirect (type $N)` where `$N` is `(func (param structref i32 i32)
// (result i32))` and pushes two `(ref $list)` values into the i32 slots: `vl check` rc 0
// over a module the engine refuses at offset 326 (`wasm-dis`, binaryen 130).
//
// THE FLOOR SAID "IS" WHERE IT MEANT "CONTAINS", which is the whole of the fix and the
// third time that one word has been the mechanism (D421's `noteBinCstr`, D422's
// `nodeTyIsTyVar`). A BARE `T` parameter has always been refused here — it matches no rung
// of `checkParams`' ladder and falls to "only i32, …, or string parameters are supported",
// measured loud at every argument rep. `a: T[]` is a `TyArray` OVER one, so
// `nodeTyIsArrayish` claimed it and the parameter was lowered at the i32 default.
//
// THE REAL FIX IS PER-PIN LIFTING and it is a monomorphizer feature, not a predicate: the
// lambda has to be instantiated once per pin with the substituted parameter types so its
// `$fnsig` key and its functype are the instance's. `scripts/silent-sweep/d426/lamgrid.py`
// prices it — 360 cells over lambda-parameter SHAPE × `T` binding × body, of which 33 were
// check-clean invalid wasm and **every one of the 33 has a CONTROL THAT RUNS**: the
// identical program with the lambda's annotation written out at the binding's own concrete
// type. That is a lost LOWERING, so this fixture is a floor and not a close.
//
// THE PRICE IS FOUR CELLS AND IT IS KEPT WHOLE at `distilled/named/d426nul_*.vl`: a
// `T | null` lambda parameter runs today at `T = boolean` and at `T = K` for a string
// literal union, because `boolean | null` and `K | null` both rep as the plain i32 the
// unsubstituted `T | null` defaults to. Nothing in the program states that coincidence and
// one binding away it is invalid wasm, so the floor refuses it with the rest.

function opT<T>(a: T[], b: T[]): boolean {
  const g = (x: T[], y: T[]) => x == y
  return g(a, b)
}

function cell(): boolean {
  const a: i32[] = [1]
  const b: i32[] = [1]
  return opT(a, b)
}

print(cell())
